14:T4e5,Most rejected proposals fail in the same place: the research question. Not because the topic is uninteresting, but because the question is unanswerable, unmeasurable, or already answered.

## Topic, problem, question

A topic is a subject area. A problem is a tension inside that area — something unresolved, contradictory or unmeasured. A question is a specific, testable formulation of that tension.

- Topic: remote work and productivity.
- Problem: studies disagree on the direction and size of the effect.
- Question: under which task types does remote work change measured output for knowledge workers?

## Three filters

1. **Reachability** — can you obtain the data, sample or documents within your timeframe?
2. **Measurability** — is there a defensible operational definition for each construct?
3. **Contribution** — if answered, does something change for a reader, a policy or a field?

> A question that passes two filters is a chapter. A question that passes three is a thesis.

## Then reverse-engineer the method

Once the question is fixed, the methodology writes itself: the design follows the question type, the sample follows the population, the analysis follows the construct definitions. That is the order reviewers expect.5:["$","$L13",null,{"post":{"id":"p_research-question-that-survives-review","slug":"research-question-that-survives-review","title":{"en":"Designing a Research Question That Survives Review","ne":"समीक्षा टिक्ने अनुसन्धान प्रश्न कसरी बनाउने"},"excerpt":{"en":"A research question is not a topic. It is a claim about what is unknown, why it matters, and how it can be answered with the data you can actually reach.","ne":"अनुसन्धान प्रश्न विषय होइन। यो के अज्ञात छ, किन महत्त्वपूर्ण छ, र कुन डाटाले उत्तर दिन सकिन्छ भन्ने दाबी हो।"},"content":{"en":"$14","ne":"धेरैजसो अस्वीकृत प्रस्ताव एउटै ठाउँमा असफल हुन्छन्: अनुसन्धान प्रश्न। विषय कमजोर भएकोले होइन, प्रश्न अनुत्तरणीय, अपरिमेय वा पहिल्यै उत्तरित भएकोले।\n\n## विषय, समस्या, प्रश्न\n\nविषय एउटा क्षेत्र हो। समस्या त्यस क्षेत्रभित्रको तनाव हो। प्रश्न त्यस तनावको विशिष्ट र परीक्षणयोग्य रूप हो।\n\n## तीन फिल्टर\n\n1. **पहुँच** — तोकिएको समयमा डाटा वा नमूना प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ?\n2. **मापनयोग्यता** — प्रत्येक कन्स्ट्रक्टको रक्षा गर्न सकिने परिभाषा छ?\n3. **योगदान** — उत्तर मिलेमा पाठक, नीति वा क्षेत्रमा केही परिवर्तन हुन्छ?\n\n> दुई फिल्टर पास गर्ने प्रश्न एउटा अध्याय हो। तीनै पास गर्ने प्रश्न थेसिस हो।"},"cover":"art:research","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Research","tags":["methodology","proposal","thesis"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-17","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":true,"seoTitle":"Designing a Research Question That Survives Review | Acttolog","seoDescription":"A research question is not a topic. It is a claim about what is unknown, why it matters, and how it can be answered with the data you can actually reach.","socialImage":""}}]
